https://github.com/MinhHaDuong/climate-finance-het/issues/1338

## Comparator design extension, 14 September 2026

Implement the 0729 decision on a wider pooled/weighted beneficiary-country
reference, with a within-country sensitivity comparison where supported. Freeze
historical country-status definitions, project strata, calendar windows, overlap
rules and weights before outcome estimation. Report effective sample size,
country/lender concentration, balance, unsupported strata and sensitivity to
excluding individual comparator countries. Retain active/cancelled observations.
Do not extrapolate silently from unsupported matches.

Following 0729's credible causal-design decision, state the exact treatment and target
population, assignment/counterfactual assumptions and policy-level uncertainty.
For pre/post designs, use contemporary untreated outcomes as well as history;
account for different adoption dates and common shocks. Check anticipation,
spillovers and concurrent policies. Good pre-period fit does not prove identification.
Do not adjust for instrument or maturity measured after treatment when estimating
the partnership's total effect; baseline matching and mediator analysis answer
different questions. Otherwise report failure to establish the causal design and seek an author scope decision; a separately labelled descriptive benchmark does not satisfy this ticket.
A formal synthetic-control study requires a supported longitudinal outcome design,
not merely a weighted pool of closed operations.

## Causal implementation gate, author decision 14 September 2026

This gate supersedes earlier optional-causal wording. Do not start primary effect
estimation until 0729 has a documented GO/NARROW design and its protocol is frozen.
Record the primary estimand/outcome/horizon, treatment rule, population, comparator
selection/weights, estimator, censoring/cancellation handling, uncertainty and
falsification/sensitivity procedures. Label exploratory changes and deviations.
A preregistration may improve transparency but cannot repair weak identification.

First design-specific test: a null-effect fixture with baseline maturity selection
and a shared calendar shock must expose the naive comparison's bias and verify
that the chosen implementation targets the declared contrast under its stated
assumptions. Add a violated-assumption fixture to demonstrate the method's limit;
simulation success is not validation of the real assignment mechanism.

Exit additions:

- [ ] 0729 causal design decision and immutable protocol recorded before primary estimation
- [ ] Cohort and estimator implement the same treatment, time zero and target population
- [ ] Design-appropriate placebo/falsification, sensitivity and treatment-level uncertainty reported
- [ ] Main effect and uncertainty reproducible, including null/adverse outcomes; no causal claim based on matching alone
- [ ] Identification failures trigger a recorded author scope decision, not an unannounced descriptive substitution
